// fix_last_m used to sit here, finding the last must-move event; it was
// called exactly once, as the last action of fix_plan (../../walk/roots/simple.id),
// and now chains there directly.

// Calls first: whether a trapping read or an import moves depends on which
// calls do.
fix_mark_moves(int last) {
  fix_mark_cls(last, 1);
  fix_mark_rest(last);
} return void;

// One entry per event, pushed by fix_push4 (../../walk/kind/push.id) and set
// by fix_mark_cls (one.id), whose whole effect is that lset: only a reader of
// this column can see either happen. Filed here rather than beside its export
// in ../../walk/roots/reset/narrow.id, which is at its three-function cap in
// a directory at its three-entry one.
fixe_mv_len() {
  int n = len((import fixe_mv));
} return int n;
given fix_fixture ():(0)
